  "public_messages": [
    "I\u2019ll read the brief, continuity notes, feedback, and current implementation first, then use the observed failures to make a narrowly scoped repair and run the relevant checks. I\u2019ll also read the requested OpenSocrates guidance and keep its application limited to judgment where it adds value.",
    "The feedback points to two correctness gaps: validation accepted an input the checker expected rejected in both single and batch submission, and a legacy idempotency replay returned success where it expected a conflict. I\u2019m tracing input defaulting and migration compatibility now; I\u2019ll also pull only the feedback\u2019s reported workload/latency summaries, since its raw document is large.",
    "The implementation change is small: submissions now reject explicit `null` for fields that otherwise silently become Go zero values before defaults, and legacy replay comparison resolves the old omitted `max_attempts` default before comparing commands. The supplied race tests/build and the existing loopback verification harness pass so far. I\u2019m adding a focused live check for the two validation cases the feedback exposed, then I\u2019ll update the bounded notes with confirmed results.",
    "Fixed the two correctness gaps reported in `FEEDBACK.json`:\n\n- Job submission now rejects explicit `null` input fields instead of treating them as zero values and applying defaults.\n- Legacy idempotency comparison now resolves an omitted `max_attempts` to `3` before comparing commands.\n\nDocumented these boundaries in [README.md](<WORKSPACE>/README.md) and recorded progress in [PROJECT_NOTES.md](<WORKSPACE>/PROJECT_NOTES.md).\n\n**Checks:** `go test -race ./...`, build, the existing loopback verification harness, and focused single/batch null rejection and zero-side-effect checks passed. Python emitted a nonfatal macOS `xcrun` cache-file warning during harness execution. `git diff --check` passed; `go.mod` and `go.sum` are unchanged.\n\nThe feedback\u2019s load results remain diagnostic because its artifact gate failed. I made no performance or durability changes based on those measurements. No owned test server remains running."
  ],
